{
  "kanji": "悪",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 悪\ntitle: bad, evil\njlpt: 4\ntags: [jlpt-n4, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 11\nradical: 心\nradicalNumber: 61\nonyomi: [アク, オ]\nkunyomi: [わる.い, わる-, あ.し, にく.い, -にく.い, ああ, いずくに, いずくんぞ, にく.む]\ndistractors: [意, 急, 思]\n---\n\n# 悪 — bad, evil\n\n**Strokes:** 11 · **Key (radical):** 心 (heart, no. 61) · **JLPT:** N4 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n悪 marks something bad, undesirable, or morally wrong. In everyday descriptions it need not mean \"evil\": bad weather or poor health also uses this family of meanings.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** imagine the flat, barred upper part as a heavy lid over [心](心.md), making the heart feel bad. This is a memory image, not a historical explanation.\n\n## Readings\n\nThis table is selective; metadata preserves all source on/kun readings, including uncommon ones.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| アク | on | 悪意 あくい (ill will), 悪天候 あくてんこう (bad weather) |\n| わる.い | kun | [悪い](../words/悪い.md) わるい (bad) |\n| わる- | kun | 悪口 わるぐち (speaking ill of someone) |\n| あ.し | kun | 善し悪し よしあし (good and bad; merit), 悪しからず あしからず (formal: \"please do not take offence\") |\n| にく.む | kun | 悪む にくむ (to hate; older or literary spelling of 憎む) |\n| ああ | kun | classical kanbun reading only (an exclamation); not used in modern Japanese |\n| いずくに／いずくんぞ | kun | classical kanbun reading only (\"where?; how could…?\"); not used in modern Japanese |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [悪い](../words/悪い.md) わるい — bad, poor\n- 悪口 わるぐち・わるくち — insulting remarks, bad-mouthing\n- 悪意 あくい — ill will, malice\n- 悪化 あっか — getting worse\n\n## Notes\n\n悪化 is あっか, not あくか: learn the small っ in this word. For ordinary \"bad\", start with わるい rather than treating every metadata reading as an interchangeable pronunciation.\n\n[意](意.md) and [急](急.md) also have 心 below, but different upper portions. 良い よい (good), also commonly いい, contrasts with 悪い.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-08 (EDRDG; [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)).\n",
